      "what_must_be_true": "Cloud service providers must keep funding AI clusters at a rate that keeps leading-edge logic and HBM fabs at full utilization; TSMC, Samsung, SK hynix and Micron must continue to take AMAT deposition, epi, CMP, plating and eBeam steps on GAA and HBM; export licenses and China 28 nm demand must not gap the 26% China mix; and Singapore plus US manufacturing must actually convert the 2028 output-doubling plan into shipped systems."
    },
    "preview_note": "AMAT reports fiscal Q3 into the strongest AI WFE tape of the cycle. Q2 was $7.91B of revenue; the setup is a step-function in tool deliveries after customers unlocked cleanroom constraints, plus AGS still running above a 20% growth rate. Three things decide the print and the reaction: (1) whether Semiconductor Systems clears $7B on GAA plus a 50%+ YoY DRAM/HBM print; (2) whether company-level non-GAAP gross margin holds the 50% handle for a 13th consecutive YoY expansion; and (3) the Q4 guide \u2014 management has been raising CY26 Semi Systems and is signaling a $10B-plus quarter as DRAM cleanrooms open. A beat-and-raise with another year of grow-faster-than-WFE language and 2027 conviction should be taken well; a guide that only matches the Q3 run-rate, or any pullback in China/licensing commentary, would fade the multiple. Watch FCF conversion: Q2 CFO was only $845M on $2.8B of NI after working capital. A rebuild in cash conversion plus the October EPIC Center unveil frames the 2027 setup.",
    "reasoning": "The August 13 8-K already prints fiscal Q3 (ended July 26, 2026). Every Q3 line is taken from that exhibit: revenue $9,115, COS $4,529, opex $1,100/$249/$162, OI $3,075, interest $68, other income \u2212$100 (unrealized investment loss), tax $369, NI $2,538, 800M diluted shares, GAAP EPS $3.1725; CFO $3,037, D&A $151, SBC $169, residual other operating $179, capex \u2212$707, other investing \u2212$706, buybacks \u2212$440, dividends \u2212$420, other financing \u2212$29, \u0394cash +$735. Restricted-cash end is $7,094; RE rolls 59,274+2,538\u2212420\u2212440=60,952; assets/liabilities/equity match the published $43,522/$17,896/$25,626. Non-GAAP NI $2,795 is the filed recon, so adjusted EPS is 2,795/800=3.49375 ($3.50 as reported). Q4 is taken at the issued midpoint ($10,250 / $4.02) because the DRAM/GAA 2H commentary already sits inside that guide; FY26 is then YTD $24,037 plus that Q4. FY27\u201329 compound off the 8-quarter visibility, 14-week Q1, AGS mid-teens CAGR and the 2028 output-doubling plan, with WFE share held at 22% so segment dollars exactly equal market \u00d7 share. FCF conversion rebuilds after the Q2 WC hole; capital return stays 60\u201380% of FCF rather than a mechanical 100% because Q3 itself returned only 37%."
  },
